  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1510.06 Muck and Rock Management",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1510.06 Muck and Rock Management.\n\n(a) For purposes of this part, the following definitions apply:\n\n(1) “Blasted material” means all of the earth material loosened as a result of the blasting;\n\n(2) “Muck” means the blasted material remaining after the rocks have been removed; and\n\n(3) “Rocks” means the larger pieces of blasted material that are separated from the muck for use elsewhere, including for feedstock of a rock crushing operation.\n\n(b) Muck shall be removed from the blast area as soon as reasonably possible.\n\n(c) Rocks shall be managed so as to prevent water supply wells or surface waters from being contaminated by runoff.\n\nSource. #12342, eff 8-15-17; ss by #14472, eff 1-19-26, EXPIRES: 1-19-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1500.html"
